## MRE-K Loop Architecture

```
Kubernetes API → Metis (sensors) → GraphDB (knowledge base)
                                        ↓ (RabbitMQ: amocna.graph.updates)
                                   Palamedes (reasoner)
                                        ↓ queries Prometheus for metric thresholds
                                        ↓ (RabbitMQ: amocna.action.queue)
                                   Themis (executor) → Kubernetes API
                                        ↓ (RabbitMQ: amocna.status.queue)
                                   Palamedes (saga manager)
```

## Key Technologies

- **Java 25**, Spring Boot 4.0.6, Maven
- **gRPC** (Metis ingestion server on port 50052)
- **RabbitMQ** (inter-module messaging: graph updates, actions, status)
- **GraphDB** (RDF triple store, CNEEOnt ontology)
- **Fabric8** (Kubernetes client for sensors)
- **Prometheus** (metric source — queried by Palamedes, never written to GraphDB)

## Ontologies (in libs/ontology/)

- **CNEEOnt** — Cloud-Native Execution Environment Ontology (entities, states, relationships)
- **MoaMont** — Management of Autonomic Monitoring Ontology (actions, workflows)
- **BridgeOnt** — Bridge between CNEEOnt and MoaMont

## Module Communication

| From | To | Via | Message |
|---|---|---|---|
| Metis | Palamedes | RabbitMQ `amocna.graph.updates` | GraphUpdateMessage (resourceIri, changeKind) |
| Palamedes | Themis | RabbitMQ `amocna.action.queue` | ActionMessage (protocol, instruction, payload) |
| Themis | Palamedes | RabbitMQ `amocna.status.queue` | ActionStatusUpdate (actionId, status) |

## Important Notes

- Metric values are NEVER stored in GraphDB — they stay in Prometheus
- Metis observes (K8s API only) — no threshold evaluation
- Palamedes thinks (queries Prometheus, evaluates thresholds, plans actions)
- Themis executes (K8s API calls)
- GraphDB stores topology, states, and anomaly conditions
- Anomaly states are subclasses of both State and Anomaly in CNEEOnt
